WEBVTT

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.690
Either you stay
in Chronos or you die...

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.700
Choose one.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.030
I don't like either.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.370
Heartnet!

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:17.370
Go ahead and shoot
that bitch, Train.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:21.710
I don't wanna kill
or be killed.

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.610
Then, I have no choice.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.450
I won't let you get away!

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.390
What's the matter?

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:41.390
Train, why don't you shoot?

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.060
If you don't shoot, then...

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:45.730
Your opponents are right here!

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.400
Creed Diskenth!

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.070
We're taking you into custody
for treason against Chronos!

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:55.740
Come quietly.
You can't escape from us.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.680
You're taking me?

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.180
That's a laugh.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:06.020
Are you insulting the Numbers!?

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.480
Do you seriously think there's
no one stronger than the Numbers?

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:15.030
I guess an old organization
really is hopeless.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.700
Enough of your impertinence!

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.030
Let's go, Ash!

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.020
Yeah!

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:26.040
<i>That's how it always starts...</i>
<i>under the azure sky</i>

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:33.210
<i>After making a vow,</i>
<i>I now set off</i>

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:52.330
<i>Yeah, the desert glitters with a golden hue</i>
<i>(The wind is scorching)</i>

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:58.670
<i>I'm searching for a diamond flower</i>
<i>(I keep on wandering)</i>

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:05.010
<i>Now, for the first time in my life,</i>

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:11.350
<i>I live for someone else</i>

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:17.860
<i>There's something</i>
<i>I wanna protect</i>

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:24.360
<i>I'll never,</i>
<i>ever lose it again</i>

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:27.370
<i>Resound,</i>
<i>my heartbeat!</i>

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:37.370
<i>A heartbeat smaller and fragile,</i>
<i>but tougher than anyone's.</i>

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:54.220
"Targeted Cat"

00:02:54.730 --> 00:03:02.000
<i>♪ The beating of an insect's wings ♪</i>

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:09.010
<i>♪ Lightly, lightly, floating... ♪</i>

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:16.680
<i>♪ Carrying our feelings ♪</i>

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:24.360
Did you abandon your gun, Heartnet!?

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.360
I won't carry a gun any more.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.690
The Numbers' weapons are something
used for saving the world.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:33.360
While you're filled
with such self-righteousness,

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.030
how many people's blood do you think
is being spilt in this world we live in!?

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:40.370
Is it okay to kill people
if it's for justice?

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.040
Heartnet...

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.710
Leave me alone!

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.540
You are wrong!!

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:02.660
Heartnet!

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:10.670
You can't even graze me
with attacks like that.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:13.370
You won't be laughing for long!

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:29.710
What!?

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:36.030
I see... You made me
draw my <i>Kotetsu...</i>

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:39.430
I guess I have to say
"as expected from the Numbers"...

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:02.990
I guess you won't forgive me
even though I abandoned my gun...

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:05.320
You have power...

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:08.330
Even if you abandoned your gun,
being drawn by that power,

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:11.660
people like Creed will
probably flock towards you.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:15.000
You'll definitely become
a threat to Chronos.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:21.010
Those who leave Chronos will be dealt with
by Chronos... That is the code of Chronos.

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:23.010
Chronos, Chronos...

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.570
What the hell
is Chronos to you?

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.690
I believe...

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:41.030
in Chronos' ideal of righting
this troubled world.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:48.700
And, I decided that until that ideal
is realized, I'd abandon my human heart.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:52.040
Don't you get tired
from always being like that?

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.130
Realize your mistake!

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.700
Come back to Chronos!

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:10.810
I have no choice...

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.330
Ash!

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:19.330
Y- you bastard!!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:22.630
That uncanny technique is...
from Itairiku...

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.670
That's none of your business.

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:32.010
How dare you kill my partner!

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:34.350
That incompetent moron
was your partner?

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:37.350
A partner is someone like
what Train is to me,

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:40.350
and what I am to Train!

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:45.020
Now, if you don't wanna die,
beg for your life.

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:48.030
Oh? You're not gonna beg?

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:49.690
Then, I have no choice.

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:52.700
You think you've concealed
the distance with an invisible blade!?

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:54.700
With blood covering the blade,

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.700
the tip of your sword
is in plain sight!

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.700
The distance!?
The tip of my sword!?

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.640
Such things don't matter to me.

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:13.980
Don't worry.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.990
I didn't aim for your vitals.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.990
D- Damn!

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:22.990
Why were we taken out
by a lowly eraser?

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:27.330
Go back and tell
those cowardly elders...

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:30.320
that it's all over for Chronos.

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:36.660
Keep this in mind.
Times have changed.

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:44.350
And, Train isn't a member
of the Numbers any more.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:46.940
He's my partner.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:10.640
Sorry, but you're coming
with me, Train Heartnet.

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:12.310
What!?

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:14.310
Who are you!?

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:16.310
My name is Shiki.

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:17.980
I'm a Taoist.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:22.650
A Taoist!? So,
you people survived!

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:26.320
It'll take more than
Chronos to eradicate us.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:29.330
Let me show you
the Tao's power!

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:30.330
<i>Mudeka</i>!

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:32.820
Take this!
Borer Poison's Curse!

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:45.340
Now, Train Heartnet.
Come with me.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:47.340
Creed is waiting for you.

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:48.350
Creed!?

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:49.680
What's Creed planning!?

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:53.680
I don't have to explain it
to one of Chronos' dogs!

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:56.180
Train's the one
we want to talk to...

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:05.300
<i>♪ A baby's first cry ♪</i>

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:10.300
<i>♪ The beating of an insect's wings ♪</i>

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.640
What!? What happened!?

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:14.640
<i>♪ Lightly, lightly, floating... ♪</i>

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:16.640
Damn!
<i>♪ Lightly, lightly, floating... ♪</i>

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:19.980
Train's-!
<i>♪ Lightly, lightly, floating... ♪</i>

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:22.310
<i>♪ Carrying our feelings ♪</i>

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:27.320
<i>Nguita-no-gonai, nguita-no-gonai,</i>
<i>nguita-no-gonai!</i>
<i>♪ Carrying our feelings ♪</i>

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:29.980
<i>nguita-no-gonai!!</i>
<i>Nguita-no-gonai, nguita-no-gonai,</i>

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:37.320
Take this! Curse
of Flying Locusts!

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:43.670
That damn Creed!

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:47.000
When did he find an ally like that?
<i>♪ Lightly, lightly, floating... ♪</i>

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:50.670
It looks like he's up to something...
<i>♪ Lightly, lightly, floating... ♪</i>

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:51.340
<i>♪ Tomorrow, for sure... ♪</i>

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.680
I'm concerned about Creed's actions.
<i>♪ Tomorrow, for sure... ♪</i>

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:57.010
Right now, he's our priority.
<i>♪ Tomorrow, for sure... ♪</i>

00:09:57.010 --> 00:09:58.350
Well, I think we can let
XIII be free for a while.
<i>♪ Tomorrow, for sure... ♪</i>

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:02.550
<i>♪ Lightly, lightly, floating... ♪</i>
Well, I think we can let
XIII be free for a while.

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:06.010
<i>♪ Lightly, lightly, floating... ♪</i>

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:16.520
<i>♪ It will reach the sky ♪</i>

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:30.050
Hey, what are you running
so frantically for?

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:32.380
And, what's more,
your face is as black as coal.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:34.720
Oh, I got it.
You're jogging!

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:36.390
Of course not!

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:38.060
You can run pretty fast.

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:40.720
But I can run faster!

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:42.160
Do you admit defeat?

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:50.330
He's pretty good. Then, I guess
it's time for me to get serious!

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:52.930
I'll go on ahead!

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:56.570
That's nothing!

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:00.340
Ouch!

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:01.680
Oops!

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.010
I'll go on ahead!

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.500
Tada!

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:19.030
What're you busting
your butt for!?

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.030
Nothing.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:24.590
Watching you made me
want to run, that's all!

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:32.380
Here you go!
You must be thirsty!

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:33.710
I don't need it!

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:37.240
A bottle of milk after a run
tastes good too, you know...

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:45.050
Ah! That really hits the spot!

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.390
It tastes good, doesn't it?

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.060
It tastes like
it always does.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.400
You're as unfriendly as always.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.730
Wait a second, why are
you in my apartment!?

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:00.070
You made me run so much,

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.010
so let me take a break here.

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:04.680
You're the one who
followed me on your own!

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:07.340
No, no, no...
You don't understand.

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:10.680
When you enjoy something,
you should share it with a friend.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:13.020
So, lemon soda!

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:14.020
Huh?

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:16.690
You'll treat me to lemon soda!

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:19.020
I don't quite get
what you're saying...

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:22.360
There'll be a carnival
at the harbor tomorrow!

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:24.700
A celebration that
happens once a year!

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:27.030
The fireworks at the climax
of the festival are super famous.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:32.370
To tell you the truth, it's like I moved
to this town for those fireworks.

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:35.370
While watching huge fireworks
exploding with a bang,

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:38.380
you take a swig
of very cold lemon soda.

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:41.040
That's the best part
of watching fireworks!

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.710
What's that got to do with me?

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:47.150
Obviously, I'm inviting my only
friend in this town, you, Train-<i>kun,</i>

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:50.620
to the fireworks display!

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:51.890
I'm tellin' ya,

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:54.730
it's definitely more fun to watch it
with someone else, rather than by yourself!

00:12:54.730 --> 00:12:57.730
Even so, why do I have
to treat you to lemon soda?

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:00.330
It was you who lost,
right, Train-<i>kun</i>?

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:01.670
I lost?

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:03.330
The footrace!

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:07.340
The number of times
you passed me was 63 times.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:12.010
I passed you was 64 times.
The number of times

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:14.010
Therefore, I won!

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:17.140
So, lemon soda!
Okay!?

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:25.360
All right, I guess...

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:28.360
Yaay! Lemon soda!
Lemon Soda!

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:31.700
It doesn't take
much to please you...

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.760
Happiness isn't money.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:36.200
It's the free time that
you spend with your friends...

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:37.700
Something like that...

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:39.700
Also...

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:42.370
I think you should
keep this with you.

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:44.040
Why are you telling
me this now?

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:47.040
You'll be living on
your own from now on.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:50.380
So, you'll have
to protect yourself!

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:52.720
And your loved ones, too.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:54.380
I don't have anyone like that.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:56.050
Don't act so tough!

00:13:56.050 --> 00:14:00.990
Everyone makes an important friend
or two during their lives, right?

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:02.660
Well, then...

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:05.000
Are you leaving?

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:07.660
Are you asking me
to stay over night?

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:10.000
No way!

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:13.670
You'd better hurry up
and move out of this place.

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:17.340
Apparently, you're popular, so...

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:20.010
Well, then, I'll meet you
at the pier tomorrow evening.

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:23.340
I'll find the best spot
for watching the fireworks display.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:28.350
Stop it!
It's no use.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:29.690
What?

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:31.690
I'm saying it's no use!

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:35.030
Why!? You told me
to bring him earlier, and...

00:14:35.030 --> 00:14:38.520
Right, but I'm telling you,
it's no use for now...

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:45.370
...while he's being
deluded by that woman...

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:48.000
By... that witch!

00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:59.720
Eve!

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:07.020
Is it interesting? That, "101 Wild
Elephants on The Stampede!" book...

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:10.990
What's that?

00:15:10.990 --> 00:15:14.330
It means that there's
going to be fireworks.

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:15.670
Fireworks...

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:18.000
Well, you know...

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:22.010
Fireworks are shot into the air,

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:27.680
there's a 'kaboom' noise...
and the night sky becomes bright.

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:28.680
Are they weapons?

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:30.010
Whoa!

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:33.680
No, they aren't...
Well, you know...

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:36.350
They're exploding art.

00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:38.360
They're pretty.

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:43.360
Colorful lights spread out
in a round shape, and...

00:15:43.360 --> 00:15:44.360
I wanna see them...

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:45.700
Huh?

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:48.370
I wanna see...
a fireworks display...

00:15:48.370 --> 00:15:50.030
That wouldn't be good.

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:53.700
If the people who're after us
find us or something...

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:55.710
Looks like they've
already found us.

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:57.370
I don't know them.

00:15:57.370 --> 00:16:00.310
A man and a woman with a child
should be staying at your place.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:03.310
It's in your best interest
to tell us the truth.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:05.320
Why don't you suit yourself
and search the house?

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:07.180
The guest room is upstairs.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:13.650
This way!

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:52.030
Well...

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:56.370
I wonder if this isn't a very
good match for fireworks...

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:57.800
Oh, well!

00:17:00.300 --> 00:17:04.070
Hmm, I might have come too early...

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:16.120
Leave it to me!

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:21.250
All right!

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:28.330
Thank you!

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:32.340
Okay, then... I promised
to meet someone, so...

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:36.340
A promise...
with your boyfriend?

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:37.830
With my friend!

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:47.020
Let's see...

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:50.510
The fireworks will go up
from that area, so...

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:57.030
they'll go kaboom around here.

00:17:57.030 --> 00:18:00.290
Yep! This place may actually
be a nice little unknown spot.

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:05.530
I hope my lemon
soda comes soon...

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:10.640
Who...

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:11.980
...are you?

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:13.980
Oh, I see!

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.980
You're a friend
of Train-<i>kun's</i>, right!?

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:18.980
Me, too!

00:18:18.980 --> 00:18:20.980
That's great!

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:25.320
Thanks to you, Train-<i>kun</i>
has become quite cheerful...

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:27.990
You've got an invisible sword?

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:30.660
That's a rare technique you use...

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:34.660
Living a free and easy life...

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:36.670
What's wrong with it?

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:43.010
Wh- why don't you...
let Train-<i>kun</i>... have... his own way?

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:44.500
Yaay!

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:53.670
Wait! Don't harm the children!

00:18:54.680 --> 00:19:00.620
Darn! I can't...
move my body...

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:04.390
If I can just...
move my arm...

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:23.850
G- get out of here! Now!!

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:30.320
Don't underestimate me...

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:34.850
I'm not working alone
as a sweeper for nothing.

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:44.000
<i>He's walking!</i>

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:48.840
<i>But my "Reflect Shot"</i>
<i>was perfect! It hit his leg!</i>

00:19:58.350 --> 00:20:02.020
To My Dear Friend Train,

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:06.550
I'll release you from that
witch's spell tonight.

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:12.030
This way!

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:15.520
The lady... The lady
in <i>yukata</i> was...

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:21.040
Lady...

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:24.710
Hi, Train!
You can rest easy now.

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:30.380
I've just taken care of the witch
who's been deluding you.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:32.710
Now, you can join me-

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:40.720
Train-<i>kun...</i>

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:43.730
Don't talk.

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:46.400
Are the children-?

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:50.070
Don't worry.
They're all right.

00:20:50.070 --> 00:20:53.400
I really screwed up.

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:56.740
Forget that, just don't talk!

00:20:56.740 --> 00:21:00.680
So you brought it with you...

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:05.350
Don't ever give it up, okay?

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:11.020
I'm sure you'll be able to use it
for the right reasons, so...

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:14.360
I- idiot! Don't say things
that sound like parting words!

00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:17.350
I wanted to drink...
lemon soda...

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:29.040
Fireworks...

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:31.030
they're pretty...

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:38.050
Saya...

00:21:38.050 --> 00:21:41.540
So, the witch who was
leading you astray died, huh?

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:48.060
Now release yourself
from that witch's spell

00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:50.060
and go back to being
the old Train!

00:21:50.060 --> 00:21:52.400
Bastard...

00:21:52.400 --> 00:21:55.060
You bastard...

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:59.070
You bastard, I'll make
you pay for this!!

00:21:59.070 --> 00:22:01.000
Train!

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:03.670
You still haven't awakened yet?

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:07.340
I swear I'll make you
pay for this!!

00:22:15.320 --> 00:22:20.350
<i>The stars in the night sky</i>
<i>are my tears</i>

00:22:20.350 --> 00:22:24.360
<i>Goddess of the moon,</i>
<i>angel of the stars!</i>

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:30.130
<i>Please stop time tonight!</i>

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:45.050
<i>Please show yourself,</i>
<i>even if just a little</i>

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:50.820
<i>Around the time the first evening star</i>
<i>appears, I hear footsteps approaching</i>

00:22:50.820 --> 00:22:56.720
<i>The only time I can see you</i>
<i>is when the moon is shining</i>

00:22:56.720 --> 00:22:59.730
<i>Please let me dream a little</i>

00:22:59.730 --> 00:23:02.960
<i>'Cause it'll become</i>
<i>an illusion by morning</i>

00:23:02.960 --> 00:23:06.330
<i>Even though I know it,</i>
<i>I still feel lonely</i>

00:23:06.330 --> 00:23:12.010
<i>The stars in the night sky</i>
<i>are my tears</i>

00:23:12.010 --> 00:23:18.010
<i>You held me in your arms</i>
<i>and your passionate lips met mine</i>

00:23:18.010 --> 00:23:21.010
<i>Please don't let go of me</i>

00:23:21.010 --> 00:23:24.350
<i>I'm about to melt in your arms</i>

00:23:24.350 --> 00:23:27.190
<i>But morning is almost here</i>

00:23:27.190 --> 00:23:30.690
<i>Goddess of the moon,</i>
<i>angel of the stars!</i>

00:23:30.690 --> 00:23:37.030
<i>I pray to you,</i>
<i>please stop time</i>

00:23:44.370 --> 00:23:45.710
"Next Episode"

00:23:45.710 --> 00:23:47.040
This is Eve.
"Next Episode"

00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:51.040
I'm at the fireworks
display right now.

00:23:51.040 --> 00:23:53.710
Sven says they're very pretty,

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:56.380
but I've been having this uneasy
feeling for a little while now...

00:23:56.380 --> 00:23:58.390
The smell of something...

00:23:58.390 --> 00:24:01.990
Yes... It's the smell of blood...

00:24:01.990 --> 00:24:06.390
That man... It seems like
Black Cat is nearby...

00:24:06.390 --> 00:24:08.000
"Badly Wounded Cat"

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:09.330
Was that fireworks?
"Badly Wounded Cat"
